# SQL's `NOT` in capitals: DS0105 with a fix to `not`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where NOT isnull(amount)
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..40
  PIPELINE@0..39
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..39
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      PREFIX_EXPR@21..39
        IDENT@21..24 "NOT"
        WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
        CALL_EXPR@25..39
          NAME_REF@25..31
            IDENT@25..31 "isnull"
          ARG_LIST@31..39
            L_PAREN@31..32 "("
            NAME_REF@32..38
              IDENT@32..38 "amount"
            R_PAREN@38..39 ")"
  WHITESPACE@39..40 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `NOT` in capitals
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where NOT isnull(amount)
  |                      ^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `not`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where not isnull(amount)
which parses without errors
